🔹 1. Difference between relative, absolute, fixed, sticky positioning ?
relative: positioned relative to its normal position.
absolute: positioned relative to the nearest positioned ancestor (not static).
fixed: positioned relative to the viewport, doesn’t move on scroll.
sticky: behaves like relative until a scroll threshold, then sticks like fixed.

🔹 2. Difference between inline, block, and inline-block
inline: no line break, only occupies content width (e.g., <span>).
block: takes full width, starts on a new line (e.g., <div>).
inline-block: behaves inline but allows setting width/height.

🔹 4. Difference between relative units (em, rem, %, vh/vw) ?
em: relative to parent element’s font-size.
rem: relative to root (html) font-size.
%: relative to parent’s dimensions.
vh, vw: relative to viewport height/width.

🔹5. Explain Flexbox vs Grid ?
Flexbox → one-dimensional layout (row or column). Best for navbars, buttons, aligning items.
Grid → two-dimensional layout (rows + columns). Best for page layouts, dashboards.

🔹 9. Responsive Design (Media Queries) ?
@media (max-width: 768px) {
  body { background-color: lightblue; }
}

🔹 10. Difference between inline CSS, internal CSS, external CSS    
Inline → inside HTML element (<div style="color:red">).
Internal → inside <style> tag in HTML head.
External → separate .css file linked with <link>.

🔹How do you achieve responsiveness in CSS?

Media queries (@media)
Relative units (em, rem, %, vh, vw)
Flexbox/Grid
Mobile-first design


